      "name": "Titanic Grasp",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The titan makes a fist Strike against a creature affected by their impossible stature, even if it's outside of the titan's normal reach. On a hit, the titan automatically Grabs the creature and, if out of their reach, pulls it within reach."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Wide Cleave",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The titan makes a melee weapon Strike against each foe within their reach. This counts as three attacks for the titan's multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until all attacks have been made."
    }
  ],
  "text": "Those titans who remained true to their creators, refusing to participate in their peers' rebellion, earned their freedom while the others were imprisoned. Many Elysian titans train aspiring champions of freedom, sacrifice, and selflessness.\n\n---\nCreated by ancient deities long before the rise of mortal ancestries, titans united and attempted to overthrow their deific progenitors. The resulting war still figures prominently throughout mortal myths, in which most titans were cast down and imprisoned for eons."
